   "etymology": "From Old Albanian kat (Gjon Buzuku 1499 – c. 1577), also attested as mkatë (Pjetër Budi 1566 — 1622) and mpkat (Pjetër Bogdani 1630—1689), from Latin peccātum (“sin, error, fault”). The origin of the initial nasal is unclear, yet it could either reflect the native preposition më (“in, on, at”) (earlier mbë, ëmbë), or be from a learned influence via Latin peccātum. Phonological development of earliest form kat from *peccátu- > *pëkát > *pkát > kat.",
